# Argocd sync

## Gate

Use when the user asks to sync, refresh, prune, run a resource action,
create/update/delete an Application, or otherwise mutate Argo CD state.
Skip pure status / tree / events asks (those stay on `argocd-apps`).

Never invent `applicationName`, `applicationNamespace`, revision, or
resource refs. Resolve from MCP this turn or from ids the user pasted.

## Prefer MCP

When an Argo CD MCP is ready, use these tools — do not invent a side CLI
while MCP works:

| Need | Tool | Gate |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Sync | `sync_application` | explicit sync/refresh verb + named app |
| Dry-run sync | `sync_application` with `dryRun=true` | prefer before live prune/sync when unsure |
| List resource actions | `get_resource_actions` | read-only discovery |
| Run resource action | `run_resource_action` | explicit action verb + named resource |
| Create Application | `create_application` | explicit create + full spec from user |
| Update Application | `update_application` | explicit update naming the app |
| Delete Application | `delete_application` | explicit delete naming the app |

Optional params on sync: `prune`, `revision`, `syncOptions`,
`applicationNamespace`, `argocdBaseUrl`. Do not enable `prune` unless the
user asked to prune or accepted prune risk this turn.

## Read-only default

List/get/tree/events/logs/projects/clusters are fine when Argo CD work is
authorized (`argocd-apps`). Do **not**:

- sync or refresh live (non-dryRun)
- prune during sync
- run a resource action (`run_resource_action`)
- create, update, or delete an Application

…unless the user gave an explicit verb this turn naming the Application
(and resource when the action is resource-scoped).

## Sync procedure

1. Resolve the app (`list_applications` / `get_application`).
2. Read status/events first when the reason for sync is unclear —
   OutOfSync alone is not permission to sync.
3. Prefer `dryRun=true` when the user is unsure, or when prune is in play.
4. Call `sync_application` only with an explicit sync/refresh verb and a
   named app. Pass `applicationNamespace` when non-default.
5. Re-read `get_application` (and tree if needed) after sync — do not
   claim Synced from the sync RPC alone when a follow-up get is cheap.
6. Report app + sync result + health honestly (Synced / OutOfSync /
   Progressing / failed).

## Resource actions

1. Discover with `get_resource_actions` using a real `resourceRef` from
   the tree — never invent actions.
2. Run `run_resource_action` only when the user named the action (or
   clearly asked to execute one listed option) and the resource.
3. Treat restart / delete-pod style actions as disruptive: state blast
   radius briefly before running when practical.

## Create / update / delete

- **Create** (`create_application`): require name, namespace, project,
  source (`repoURL` / `path` / `targetRevision`), and destination from
  the user or a pasted manifest — never invent repo URLs or destinations.
- **Update** (`update_application`): explicit update verb + named app;
  prefer showing the intended field change before applying when practical.
- **Delete** (`delete_application`): explicit delete verb + named app.
  `cascade` / `propagationPolicy` are destructive — only set when the
  user asked for cascade/orphan behavior; state that live cluster
  resources may be removed.
- Automated syncPolicy (`automated.prune` / `selfHeal`) changes are
  policy mutations — require an explicit ask, not a silent add-on to a
  status turn.

## Irreversible / blast radius

- Prune sync and cascade delete can remove live cluster objects.
- Wrong Application namespace can hit a different app with the same name.
- State the risk in one sentence when prune/cascade/delete is requested;
  proceed only when clearly authorized.

## Report shape

1. Application name + namespace
2. Action taken (dry-run sync / sync / action / create / update / delete)
3. Post-read sync + health (or delete confirmation)
4. Short failure signal when unsuccessful (event / message, redacted)
5. Stop — do not chain unrelated mutates

## Refuse

- Mass-sync "all apps" or sync every OutOfSync app without each being
  named or clearly in scope
- Invented revisions, prune flags, or cascade defaults
- Pasting repo credentials, tokens, or private kubeconfig material from
  Application secrets into chat
